===== UC-sales-person-login-sales-person bad_example | no `Spec.post { … } { … }` with named-field records found
values: None
```lean
-- why: The output incorrectly states that the Sales Person is signed in, even though the entered password is incorrect.
example : Spec.pre IN ∧ ¬ Spec.post IN OUT := by
  unfold Spec
  let i := { username := "john_doe", password := "wrong_password", accounts := [Account.{ username := "john_doe", password := "correct_password", email := "john@example.com" }]}
  let o := { signedIn := true }
  decide
```

In this example, the input `i` satisfies `Spec.pre` because the username and password are not empty. However, the output `o` incorrectly states that the Sales Person is signed in, even though the entered password is incorrect. This is a violation of the requirement, as the system should not log in the Sales Person with an incorrect password.
